Maybe print.lavaan.parameterEstimates() shouldn't choose at all whether to show a subset of columns.  There are other things the user can choose that would make the summary() output "too wide" (e.g., a high nd=, or adding ci=TRUE and standardized=TRUE), which lavaan doesn't try to anticipate.

I think the solution is to just update the default output when TRUE.  When it checks for any "x" variables when fixed.x=TRUE, instead of adding "std.nox" to the list, it could replace "std.all" (and "std.lv <http://std.lv>" remains in either default).  If people want both, they can explicitly request both, and they will be printed.

