#>         visual textul speed
#> visual   0.000  0.000     0
#> textual  0.511  0.000     0
#> speed    0.000  0.188     0
```

<sup>Created on 2025-04-30 with [reprex v2.1.1](https://reprex.tidyverse.org)</sup>

The lavInspect() function can print a lot of useful and interesting things, including the information matrices. See the sections on "information" in the help page on what it can print about the information matrices:

https://rdrr.io/cran/lavaan/man/lavInspect.html

For teaching, I wrote a simple function to insert the lavaan-syntax names of parameters in the lavaan matrices:

https://sfcheung.github.io/semhelpinghands/reference/annotate_matrices.html

It is only for teaching, and so it only supports simple models, though good enough for my case.

Hope this helps.

-- Shu Fai

