Books on maximum likelihood estimation will cover the distinction, but may not be specifically about the case of SEM. You may find this paper useful:

Savalei, V. (2010). Expected versus observed information in SEM with incomplete normal and nonnormal data. Psychological Methods, 15(4), 352–367. https://doi.org/10.1037/a0020143

Although this paper focuses on missing data, the "ML Inference and Information Matrix: Overview" section provides a brief overview of the two types of information matrices.

Hope this helps.

-- Shu Fai

